@base = http://localhost:5121
@alice = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@bob = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
@carla = 33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333
@yuki = 55555555-5555-5555-5555-555555555555
@mallory = 66666666-6666-6666-6666-666666666666

### Requesting a transfer = publishing ONE event. Response 202: the rest happens without the caller, and without anyone to drive it.
POST {{base}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "{{alice}}", "target": "{{carla}}", "amount": 100 }

### The state (rebuilt by the Tracking service) and the history: each event, who published it, in reaction to what
### (replace the identifier with the one from the previous response)
GET {{base}}/transfers/v-00000000

### ?wait=true: wait for the end, for the convenience of the demo
POST {{base}}/transfers?wait=true
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "{{alice}}", "target": "{{carla}}", "amount": 100 }

### Compliance refusal (blocklist): it is the Accounts service which, listening to this refusal, releases the reservation
POST {{base}}/transfers?wait=true
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "{{alice}}", "target": "{{mallory}}", "amount": 50 }

### Exchange failure (currency not quoted): same compensation, triggered by another event
POST {{base}}/transfers?wait=true
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "{{alice}}", "target": "{{yuki}}", "amount": 100 }

### Insufficient balance: the process stops from the first reaction
POST {{base}}/transfers?wait=true
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "{{bob}}", "target": "{{alice}}", "amount": 900 }

### ─── A human wait ───

### Beyond 10,000 €: waiting for an analyst; 15,000 € stay reserved
POST {{base}}/transfers?wait=true
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "{{alice}}", "target": "{{bob}}", "amount": 15000 }

###
GET {{base}}/compliance/pending

### The decision (replace the identifier): an event coming from a human
POST {{base}}/compliance/v-00000000/decision
Content-Type: application/json

{ "approved": true }

### ─── When a service goes down ───

### The exchange breaks down…
POST {{base}}/chaos
Content-Type: application/json

{ "exchangeDown": true }

### … the transfer is left hanging (status InProgress), nobody is told
POST {{base}}/transfers?wait=true
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "{{alice}}", "target": "{{bob}}", "amount": 200 }

### The only clues: the dead letters, and the transfers without recent activity
GET {{base}}/bus/dead-letters

###
GET {{base}}/transfers/stuck?delaySeconds=5

### 30 s later, the Accounts service releases the reservation by itself (status Abandoned)
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{alice}}

###
POST {{base}}/chaos
Content-Type: application/json

{ "exchangeDown": false }

### The email server fails 3 times: the bus retries (after the point of no return, nothing is undone)
POST {{base}}/chaos
Content-Type: application/json

{ "notificationFailures": 3 }

###
POST {{base}}/transfers?wait=true
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "{{alice}}", "target": "{{bob}}", "amount": 10 }

### ─── The map of the system ───

### Who listens to what: the only overview of the process, and it only exists at run time
GET {{base}}/bus

### The service added afterwards, without touching the others
GET {{base}}/loyalty/{{alice}}

###
GET {{base}}/bus/log?last=30
